data.content:
Created both files. Here's the design:

- **`SortableList.razor`** — Renders each item via `ItemTemplate`, with **Move Up / Move Down** buttons that auto-disable at boundaries.
- **`SortableList.razor.cs`** — Generic (`TItem`) code-behind. Copies the incoming `Items` list in `OnParametersSet` so the original is never mutated. After each swap, fires `OnOrderChanged` with a read-only snapshot.

**Usage** matches your example — the parent handles `OnOrderChanged` to receive the reordered list:

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> updated)
    {
        tasks = updated.ToList();
    }
}
```
